# ─── Optional mod-catalog API credentials ─────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` (which is git-ignored — see .gitignore) and fill in
# real values. Secrets are read from the ENVIRONMENT only; they are NEVER
# hard-coded, logged, or committed. Do not paste real keys into this file.

# Modrinth Personal Access Token (OPTIONAL).
# The public read endpoints used in Phase 0 (search / versions / hash lookup)
# work WITHOUT a token. A token only raises rate limits and unlocks private
# content. Create one at https://modrinth.com/settings/pats (read scopes are
# enough). When set, the Modrinth provider sends it in the `Authorization` header.
MODRINTH_API_TOKEN=

# CurseForge API key (OPTIONAL; used only once the CurseForge provider lands in a
# later phase — see docs/DOMAIN-KNOWLEDGE.md §3.2). Sent as the `x-api-key` header.
CURSEFORGE_API_KEY=

# ─── Optional LLM provider credentials ────────────────────────────────────────
# NVIDIA NIM API key (OPTIONAL; required only to use the NVIDIA chat-model provider
# — spec 0009). Create one at https://build.nvidia.com (Account → API Keys). Sent
# as the `Authorization: Bearer <key>` header; read from the ENVIRONMENT only,
# never hard-coded, logged, or committed.
NVIDIA_API_KEY=
